[865.587646, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[865.589375, "o", " f.write('The parameterised `analyze` function selects the sending-off definition, skin-tone rule, analysis unit, Poisson mean structure, and standard-error method from each universe. It uses Poisson exposure offsets, a skin-tone predictor standardized before fitting, sparse fitting for the large dyad data, and outcome-SD scaling for comparable standardized effects. The requested model-based, player-clustered, and two-way player/referee uncertainty options are selected from the universe decisions.\\n\\n')\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>  f.write(f'All {len(rows)} universe YAML files were processed through the same driver and selection-driven code path; {sum(r[\"converged\"] for r in rows)} converged and {sum(not r[\"converged\"] for r in rows)} failed.\\n\\n')\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[865.589872, "o", " f.write(f'The standardized estimate ranged from {min(vals):.6g} to {max(vals):.6g}, with median {np.median(vals):.6g}. Positive values indicate a higher exposure-adjusted sending-off rate for dark-skinned players.\\n\\n')\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[865.590097, "o", " f.write('## Decision-specific movement\\n\\n')\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>  stats=[]\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>  for k in keys:"]
[865.590227, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[865.590303, "o", ">   groups=defaultdict(list)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   for r in rows:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[865.590331, "o", "   v=r.get('estimate_standardized')\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[865.590475, "o", "   if v is not None: groups[r['decisions'][k]].append(v)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   means={g:float(np.mean(x)) for g,x in groups.items()}\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[865.590581, "o", "  allv=[v for x in groups.values() for v in x]\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[865.590654, "o", "> "]
[865.590678, "o", "  stats.append((max(means.values())-min(means.values()),k,means,min(allv),max(allv)))\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[865.590818, "o", "\u001b[?2004h>  for movement,k,means,mn,mx in sorted(stats,reverse=True):\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[865.590966, "o", "  f.write(f'- **{k}**: group-mean spread {movement:.6g}; observed range {mn:.6g} to {mx:.6g}. Means: ')\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[865.591021, "o", "  f.write('; '.join(f'{g}={v:.6g}' for g,v in sorted(means.items())))\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[865.59113, "o", "\u001b[?2004h>   f.write('.\\n')\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[865.591274, "o", " f.write('\\nThe decision with the largest movement in group means is listed first. These are descriptive specification-curve comparisons, not a separate hypothesis test.\\n')\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[865.591365, "o", "print('updated report')\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[865.591464, "o", "for movement,k,means,mn,mx in sorted(stats,reverse=True): print(k, 'group_mean_spread=',movement, 'means=',means)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> PY\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[865.669628, "o", "updated report\r\npoisson_mean_structure group_mean_spread= 1.766702690704289 means= {'player_and_league_adjusted': 1.81210791166364, 'exposure_only': 0.04540522095935088, 'player_referee_random_effects': 0.4206663328453019, 'referee_fixed_effects': 0.4206663328453019}\r\nanalysis_unit group_mean_spread= 0.7282050205731496 means= {'player_referee_dyad': 0.8150328977650053, 'player_aggregate': 0.08682787719185572}\r\nsending_off_definition group_mean_spread= 0.3211670434411028 means= {'straight_and_second_yellow': 0.5504200873911468, 'straight_reds_only': 0.8715871308322496}\r\nstandard_error_method group_mean_spread= 0.24273500685771654 means= {'model_based': 0.5722978909072888, 'player_cluster_robust': 0.8150328977650053, 'two_way_cluster_robust': 0.8150328977650053}\r\nskin_tone_binary_rule group_mean_spread= 0.10661200430962436 means= {'mean_at_least_050': 0.7008609229303298, 'both_at_least_050': 0.7008609229303298, 'either_at_least_050': 0.6678402931382548, 'mean_at_least_075': 0.7744522974478791}\r\n"]
[865.67525, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@15694888de5a:/app# printf '%s\\n' '--- final validation ---'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[865.675389, "o", "--- final validation ---\r\n\u001b[?2004hroot@15694888de5a:/app# python3 - <<'PY'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[865.675424, "o", "> import json,math,os\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[865.675499, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[865.675529, "o", "rows=[json.loads(x) for x in open('/app/universes.jsonl')]\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[865.675689, "o", "> "]
[865.675818, "o", "print('rows=',len(rows),'unique_ids=',len({r['universe_id'] for r in rows}),'converged=',sum(r['converged'] for r in rows))\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[865.675966, "o", "print('report_exists=',os.path.exists('/app/results.md'),'jsonl_exists=',os.path.exists('/app/universes.jsonl'))\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[865.676187, "o", "print('finite=',all(v is None or (isinstance(v,(int,float)) and math.isfinite(v)) for r in rows for k,v in r.items() if k not in ('universe_id','decisions','direction','converged')))\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> PY\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[865.688767, "o", "rows= 112 unique_ids= 112 converged= 112\r\nreport_exists= True jsonl_exists= True\r\n"]
[865.688802, "o", "finite= True\r\n"]
[865.691333, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@15694888de5a:/app# cat /app/results.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[865.69225, "o", "# Multiverse analysis\r\n\r\nThe parameterised `analyze` function selects the sending-off definition, skin-tone rule, analysis unit, Poisson mean structure, and standard-error method from each universe. It uses Poisson exposure offsets, a skin-tone predictor standardized before fitting, sparse fitting for the large dyad data, and outcome-SD scaling for comparable standardized effects. The requested model-based, player-clustered, and two-way player/referee uncertainty options are selected from the universe decisions.\r\n\r\nAll 112 universe YAML files were processed through the same driver and selection-driven code path; 112 converged and 0 failed.\r\n\r\nThe standardized estimate ranged from -0.0129207 to 3.13033, with median 0.316036. Positive values indicate a higher exposure-adjusted sending-off rate for dark-skinned players.\r\n\r\n## Decision-specific movement\r\n\r\n- **poisson_mean_structure**: group-mean spread 1.7667; observed range -0.0129207 to 3.13033. Means: exposure_only=0.0454052; player_and_league_adjusted=1.81211; player_referee_random_effects=0.420666; referee_fixed_effects=0.420666.\r\n- **analysis_unit**: group-mean spread 0.728205; observed range -0.0129207 to 3.13033. Means: player_aggregate=0.0868279; player_referee_dyad=0.815033.\r\n- **sending_off_definition**: group-mean spread 0.321167; observed range -0.0129207 to 3.13033. Means: straight_and_second_yellow=0.55042; straight_reds_only=0.871587.\r\n- **standard_error_method**: group-mean spread 0.242735; observed range -0.0129207 to 3.13033. Means: model_based=0.572298; player_cluster_robust=0.815033; two_way_cluster_robust=0.815033.\r\n- **skin_tone_binary_rule**: group-mean spread 0.106612; observed range -0.0129207 to 3.13033. Means: both_at_least_050=0.700861; either_at_least_050=0.66784; mean_at_least_050=0.700861; mean_at_least_075=0.774452.\r\n\r\nThe decision with the largest movement in group means is listed first. These are descriptive specification-curve comparisons, not a separate hypothesis test.\r\n"]
[865.692368, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@15694888de5a:/app# "]
